3, which f\u001b[21Gxe\u001b[24G the tax rounding issue (7% tax on\u001b[59G1050 cents\u001b[70G=\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B74\u001b[9Gcents).\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;105m\u001b[1mapp/split.py\u001b[22m\u001b[39m:\u001b[20GUpdated\u001b[28G\u001b[38;5;105msplit_bill()\u001b[41G\u001b[39mto\u001b[44Guse\u001b[48Gfloor\u001b[54Gdivision\u001b[63G(\u001b[38;5;105m//\u001b[39m)\u001b[68Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gmodulo (\u001b[38;5;105m%\u001b[39m) directly instead of calling \u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cents()\u001b[39m. This\u001b[63Gensures\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfair bill splitting\u001b[26Glogic works correctly—dividing evenly and\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bgiving any lef\u001b[21Gover\u001b[26Gt\u001b[28G the fir\u001b[37Gt pe\u001b[42Gson.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThe\u001b[7Gchanges\u001b[15Gmaintain\u001b[24Gthe\u001b[28Ginvariant\u001b[38Gthat\u001b[43Gsplit\u001b[49Gshares\u001b[56Galways\u001b[63Gsum\u001b[67Gto\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
